tch\"\n}\nrun_trace/galaxy_tool_run_006/validation_response.json\n{\n  \"action\": \"/tool_runner/index\",\n  \"citations\": true,\n  \"creator\": [\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Organization\",\n      \"name\": \"European Galaxy Team\",\n      \"url\": \"https://galaxyproject.org/eu/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Person\",\n      \"familyName\": \"Gr\\u00fcning\",\n      \"givenName\": \"Bj\\u00f6rn\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/bgruening\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Person\",\n      \"familyName\": \"Gordon\",\n      \"givenName\": \"Assaf\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/agordon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Person\",\n      \"familyName\": \"Bernt\",\n      \"givenName\": \"Matthias\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/bernt-matthias/\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"credentials\": [],\n  \"description\": \"parts of text\",\n  \"display\": true,\n  \"edam_operations\": [],\n  \"edam_topics\": [],\n  \"enctype\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n  \"errors\": {},\n  \"form_style\": \"regular\",\n  \"has_parameters\": true,\n  \"help\": \"<p><strong>What it does</strong></p>\\n<p>This tool finds $ replaces text in an input dataset.</p>\\n<p class=\\\"infomark\\\">The <strong>pattern to find</strong> can be a simple text string, or a perl <strong>regular expression</strong> string (depending on <em>pattern is a regex</em> check-box).</p>\\n<p class=\\\"infomark\\\">When using regular expressions, the <strong>replace pattern</strong> can contain back-references ( e.g. \\\\1 )</p>\\n<p class=\\\"infomark\\\">This tool uses <a class=\\\"reference external\\\" href=\\\"https://perldoc.perl.org/perlre\\\">Perl regular expression</a> syntax.</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Examples of *regular-expression* Find Patterns</strong></p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li><strong>HELLO</strong>     The word 'HELLO' (case sensitive).</li>\\n<li><strong>AG.T</strong>      The letters A,G followed by any single character, followed by the letter T.</li>\\n<li><strong>A{4,}</strong>     Four or more consecutive A's.</li>\\n<li><strong>chr2[012]\\\\t</strong>       The words 'chr20' or 'chr21' or 'chr22' followed by a tab character.</li>\\n<li><strong>hsa-mir-([^ ]+)</strong>        The text 'hsa-mir-' followed by one-or-more non-space characters. When using parenthesis, the matched content of the parenthesis can be accessed with <strong>1</strong> in the <strong>replace</strong> pattern.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p><strong>Examples of Replace Patterns</strong></p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li><strong>WORLD</strong>  The word 'WORLD' will be placed whereever the find pattern was found.</li>\\n<li><strong>FOO-$&amp;-BAR</strong>  Each time the find pattern is found, it will be surrounded with 'FOO-' at the begining and '-BAR' at the end. <strong>$&amp;</strong> (dollar-ampersand) represents the matched find pattern.</li>\\n<li><strong>$1</strong>   The text which matched the first parenthesis in the Find Pattern.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Find Pattern:</strong> HELLO\\n<strong>Replace Pattern:</strong> WORLD\\n<strong>Regular Expression:</strong> no\\n<strong>Replace what:</strong> entire line</p>\\n<p>Every time the word HELLO is found, it will be replaced with the word WORLD.</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Find Pattern:</strong> ^chr\\n<strong>Replace Pattern:</strong> (empty)\\n<strong>Regular Expression:</strong> yes\\n<strong>Replace what:</strong> column 11</p>\\n<p>If column 11 (of every line) begins with ther letters 'chr', they will be removed. Effectively, it'll turn &quot;chr4&quot; into &quot;4&quot; and &quot;chrXHet&quot; into &quot;XHet&quot;</p>\\n<hr class=\\\"docutils\\\" />\\n<p><strong>Perl's Regular Expression Syntax</strong></p>\\n<p>The Find &amp; Replace tool searches the data for lines containing or not containing a match to the given pattern. A Regular Expression is a pattern descibing a certain amount of text.</p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li><strong>( ) { } [ ] . * ? + \\\\ ^ $</strong> are all special characters. <strong>\\\\</strong> can be used to &quot;escape&quot; a special character, allowing that special character to be searched for.</li>\\n<li><strong>^</strong> matches the beginning of a string(but not an internal line).</li>\\n<li><strong>(</strong> .. <strong>)</strong> groups a particular pattern.</li>\\n<li><strong>{</strong> n or n, or n,m <strong>}</strong> specifies an expected number of repetitions of the preceding pattern.<ul>\\n<li><strong>{n}</strong> The preceding item is matched exactly n times.</li>\\n<li><strong>{n,}</strong> The preceding item ismatched n or more times.</li>\\n<li><strong>{n,m}</strong> The preceding item is matched at least n times but not more than m times.</li>\\n</ul>\\n</li>\\n<li><strong>[</strong> ... <strong>]</strong> creates a character class. Within the brackets, single characters can be placed. A dash (-) may be used to indicate a range such as <strong>a-z</strong>.</li>\\n<li><strong>.</strong> Matches any single character except a newline.</li>\\n<li><strong>*</strong> The preceding item will be matched zero or more times.</li>\\n<li><strong>?</strong> The preceding item is optional and matched at most once.</li>\\n<li><strong>+</strong> The preceding item will be matched one or more times.</li>\\n<li><strong>^</strong> has two meaning:\\n- matches the beginning of a line or string.\\n- indicates negation in a character class. For example, [^...] matches every character except the ones inside brackets.</li>\\n<li><strong>$</strong> matches the end of a line or string.</li>\\n<li><strong>\\\\|</strong> Separates alternate possibilities.</li>\\n<li><strong>\\\\d</strong> matches a single digit</li>\\n<li><strong>\\\\w</strong> matches a single letter or digit or an underscore.</li>\\n<li><strong>\\\\s</strong> matches a single white-space (space or tabs).</li>\\n</ul>\\n\",\n  \"help_format\": \"restructuredtext\",\n  \"hidden\": \"\",\n  \"hidden_versions\": [],\n  \"history_id\": \"bbd44e69cb8906b52ff12697ee535e90\",\n  \"icon\": null,\n  \"id\": \"toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/bgruening/text_processing/tp_find_and_replace/9.5+galaxy3\",\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"argument\": null,\n      \"default_value\": {\n        \"values\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721351bbde34fac114135\",\n            \"src\": \"hda\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"edam\": {\n        \"edam_data\": [\n          \"data_0006\"\n        ],\n        \"edam_formats\": [\n          \"format_2330\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"extensions\": [\n        \"txt\"\n      ],\n      \"help\": \"\",\n      \"help_format\": \"html\",\n      \"hidden\": false,\n      \"is_dynamic\": false,\n      \"label\": \"File to process\",\n      \"model_class\": \"DataToolParameter\",\n      \"multiple\": false,\n      \"name\": \"infile\",\n      \"optional\": false,\n      \"options\": {\n        \"dce\": [],\n        \"hda\": [\n          {\n            \"hid\": 6,\n            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721351bbde34fac114135\",\n            \"keep\": false,\n            \"name\": \"Cut on dataset 4\",\n            \"src\": \"hda\",\n            \"tags\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"hid\": 5,\n            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a472135cafe935e01fe3f34\",\n            \"keep\": false,\n            \"name\": \"Cut on dataset 4\",\n            \"src\": \"hda\",\n            \"tags\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"hid\": 2,\n            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a472135bbbb28ddfb96dbf0\",\n            \"keep\": false,\n            \"name\": \"ReactomePathways.gmt\",\n            \"src\": \"hda\",\n            \"tags\": []\n          }\n        ],\n        \"hdca\": [\n          {\n            \"hid\": 3,\n            \"id\": \"1c5c7891997a5f0e\",\n            \"keep\": false,\n            \"name\": \"Excel to Tabul